# Land Rover Discovery 2 five-door, 1998-2004.
#
# The second Discovery: the same basic body and 100 in wheelbase as the
# Discovery 1, with the rounded nose, the new lamps and the revised rear.
# The five-door is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Land_Rover_Discovery
#
# Dimensions 4.704 x 1.890 x 1.941 m, wheelbase 2.540 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is the side profile; the front and rear
# three-quarters show the rounded nose and the tailgate. The notes state the
# angle.
#
# Colours: grade (b), factory-derived names from a Land Rover parts
# catalogue. Epsom Green, Chawton White, Bonatti Grey and Blenheim Silver
# are common on British roads. Weights 15, 13, 12, 10, total 50, provisional.
#
# Speed 170 km/h. Comfort 75/443, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 75. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1998 intro, retires staggered 2020-2023.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/land-rover-discovery-2.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/land-rover-discovery-2.dae. References:
# citycars/references/land-rover-discovery-2/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the belt line is about 6 cm higher than the photograph,
# making the glasshouse slightly shallow; the arch cladding is a flat ribbon and
# the alpine windows are flat panels. The police livery, beacon and decal were
# deliberately omitted. At 128 px the longer rear overhang, rounded nose and
# tailgate spare read as a Discovery 2.


obj=citycar
name=LandRoverDiscovery2(EpsomGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=15
intro_year=1998
intro_month=1
retire_year=2023
retire_month=6
speed=170
length=3
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=75
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=443

